codex
A viable direction has emerged, but it is not the prior-triage “recover coordinates from a Gram matrix”: that certificate is produced directly by exact matrix factorization, and the compact route is not materially shorter. The paper’s own Section 4.2 offers a better Track B object: a rational Farkas separator for the coefficient matrix of interlacing polynomials. The checker can execute the inequalities exactly, while the standard LP method is efficient but mechanically large; I’m checking whether I can scale that native polynomial-certificate problem without turning it into generic linear algebra or leaking the separator.
