The first implementation now passes certificate construction, corruption, round-trip, guess-resistance, attack, and canonical-symmetry checks. The reference modular GCD solves 8/8 as Track B requires (about 25,000 counted field operations at the first shipping candidate), while the finite-difference route takes 23 arithmetic operations. I found and am correcting one selftest bug: the scaling gate compared the character length of two different random roots instead of comparing witness shape.
